Z||000000||86ttops||05-17-2001||11:38 AM||||Hello everyone, I am replacing my water pump and the pump has some warning slip in it about when you take off the water pump. Some of the bolts go into the timing cover it loosens the timing cover allowing coolant in the crankcase.  But it didn't mention the Fiero just several other V6 GM cars.  Is this something I really should worry about or does the timing cover have other bolts holding it on to keep it tight.||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||05-17-2001||11:51 AM||||Mine didn't but I had drained as much as possible out from the pump.  In other words, I didn't remove the block side drainplugs and that worked just fine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||05-17-2001||01:58 PM||||Its a non-issue with the Fiero. I think it was back in '81(way before EFI 2.8s or the Fiero) that they added a bolt to hold the timing cover in place when removing the pump. No worries, but both of my Feiros have an extra bolt holding the cover in place, that's why you need to remove a nut, it threads onto the cover retaining bolt. If yours has no nut to remove, watch out.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-17-2001).]||||reg||1
